_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Reassign `displayNameForNpub` when mention names change.**

`MentionTextEditingController.displayNameForNpub` only reprocesses existing draft text when the setter runs. Here the closure is memoized with `const []`, so when `mentionMembers` finishes loading you only mutate `resolveMentionDisplayNameRef` and never invoke the setter again. Any already-typed `@npub...` mention stays truncated instead of upgrading to the resolved display name.



<details>
<summary>One localized fix</summary>

```diff
-    final displayNameResolver = useMemoized<String? Function(String)>(
-      () => (npub) {
-        final hex = hexFromNpub(npub);
-        if (hex == null) return null;
-        return resolveMentionDisplayNameRef.value(hex);
-      },
-      const [],
-    );
     useEffect(() {
-      input.controller.displayNameForNpub = displayNameResolver;
+      input.controller.displayNameForNpub = (npub) {
+        final hex = hexFromNpub(npub);
+        if (hex == null) return null;
+        return resolveMentionDisplayName(hex);
+      };
       return null;
-    }, [input.controller, displayNameResolver]);
+    }, [input.controller, mentionNamesByPubkey, getAuthorMetadata]);
